      "content": "i know you're supposed to say the \"don't make a permanent decision\" thing but it doesn't feel temporary. it feels like the logical conclusion. i've fought for years and i lost. there is no more fight left in me. honestly, it feels like i've already reached the end of my rope and there's nothing on the other side. isn't it just... peaceful to think about finally being done with all this struggle? like, if everything is already gone, why keep pretending there's something left to hold onto?",
